Entries are in alphabetical order by author. Each has three parts:

- the citation, in author-date style;
- **Summary and Credibility:** what the source is, who made it and how far to trust it;
- **Relevant Content:** notes on what it means for an NYC OSPO. Items marked *Gap filled* were added from research; everything else is from Olivia's notes. Entries whose heading says (draft) were written from research and don't have Olivia's notes yet.

The GitHub repositories change over time, so their entries give an access date.
